.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt NQSINI 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqsini ,
.Nm nqvini ,
.Nm nqsupd ,
.Nm nqsfin ,
.Nm nqvfin
.Nd sign and verify a message given in pieces
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqsini
.Fa "nqsctx *c" "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "int ph"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqvini
.Fa "nqsctx *c" "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "int ph"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn nqsupd "nqsctx *c" "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t n"
.Ft int
.Fo nqsfin
.Fa "nqsctx *c"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *rnd" "size_t rndlen"
.Fa "uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqvfin
.Fa "nqsctx *c"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sig" "size_t siglen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions sign or check a message too large to hold in memory.
.Fn nqsini
starts a signature with the secret key
.Fa sk ,
.Fn nqvini
a check with the public key
.Fa pk ;
.Fa ctx ,
.Fa ctxlen
and
.Fa ph
are those of
.Xr nqsign 3 .
.Fn nqsupd
adds the next
.Fa n
bytes of the message (any number of times; an empty piece is fine).
.Fn nqsfin
writes the signature, the bytes
.Fn nqsignd
gives for the whole message with the same
.Fa rnd ,
or with
.Fa rnd
.Dv NULL
.Pq Fa rndlen No 0
a hedged one as
.Fn nqsign
makes;
.Fn nqvfin
returns what
.Fn nqvrfy
returns for the whole message.
Both take the key given at the start again, and refuse another
.Pq Er NQEARG .
For Ed25519 alone, any non-NULL
.Fa rnd
with
.Fa rndlen
0 asks for RFC 8032's deterministic signature.
.Pp
.Vt nqsctx
is sized in the header, so it can live on the stack.
It holds no pointer and no copy of the key (only its SHA3-256, to check
the key at the end), is checked on every call, and is wiped by
.Fn nqsfin
and
.Fn nqvfin
whatever they return; a context used up, never started, used in the
other direction or changed gives
.Er NQESTATE .
.Pp
What can stream:
.Bl -bullet
.It
ML-DSA, pure and pre-hash: the message representative mu is SHAKE256
over the hash of the public key, the prefix and the message, one pass;
the end goes through the external-mu signer of
.Xr nqsignmu 3 .
.It
HashSLH-DSA (any
.Fa ph ) ,
Ed25519ph and the ML-DSA + Ed25519 hybrids with
.Fa ph
.Dv NQS512 :
the hash of the message streams, and the end is the one-call signature
on it.
.El
.Pp
Pure SLH-DSA, pure Ed25519 and Ed25519ctx, Ed25519ph with another hash,
and the hybrids without SHA-512 return
.Er NQENOSUP :
their signers read the message twice (SLH-DSA its randomiser and then
its digest, Ed25519 its nonce and then its challenge), so the whole
message would have to be kept.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
An unknown
.Fa alg ,
a
.Dv NULL
pointer, a context too long, an unknown
.Fa ph ,
an
.Fa rnd
of another length, or another key at the end.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa siglen
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
A key or signature of the wrong length.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
The signature does not verify.
.It Bq Er NQESTATE
The context is not one these functions left open in this direction.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
The algorithm and mode cannot stream (above).
.It Bq Er NQEFLT , NQERNG
As
.Xr nqsign 3 .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nqsctx c;
uint8_t buf[65536], sig[3309];
size_t n, got;
int rc = nqsini(&c, NQMLDSA65, sk, sklen, NULL, 0, 0);
while (rc == NQOK && (n = fread(buf, 1, sizeof buf, f)) > 0)
  rc = nqsupd(&c, buf, n);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqsfin(&c, sk, sklen, NULL, 0, sig, sizeof sig, &got);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3 ,
.Xr nqsignmu 3
.Sh STANDARDS
FIPS 204, FIPS 205, RFC 8032.
